Answer: A class is a blueprint or template given to the JVM to create objects. It defines the structure and behavior that objects of that class will have. Example:

```java
class Dog {
String name;
String breed;
int cost;
```

void eat() {

```java
System.out.println(name + " is eating");
}
```

void sleep() {

```java
System.out.println(name + " is sleeping");
}
```

void bark() {

```java
System.out.println(name + " is barking");
}
}
```

Here, Dog is the class.

