Answer: The dot operator is used with the reference variable to access and assign values to the properties of an object. Example:

```java
Dog dog1 = new Dog();
dog1.name = "Rocky";
dog1.breed = "Bulldog";
dog1.cost = 9999;
```

Here, values are assigned to the name, breed, and cost properties of the object referred to by dog1.

Answer: The dot operator is used to access the methods of an object. Example:

```java
dog1.eat();
dog1.sleep();
dog1.bark();
```

The methods are executed using the object reference stored in dog1.

