Answer: An object with a reference stores its reference in a variable and can be accessed multiple times. Example:

```java
Dog dog1 = new Dog();
dog1.eat();
dog1.sleep();
dog1.bark();
```

An anonymous object does not store its reference and is normally used only once. Example:

```java
new Dog().bark();
```

Answer: A separate application class can be created to contain the main() method. Example:

```java
class Dog {
String name;
String breed;
int cost;
```

void eat() {

```java
